efficiently-computable isomorphism\emph{ψ} : G2 →G1 is known are called
Type 2 pairings; if such an isomorphism \emph{ψ} is not known then
\emph{e} is called a Type 3 pairing. Many cryptographic protocols in the
asymmetric setting

rely on the existence of \emph{ψ} for their security reduction while
some use it in the protocol

itself. For these reasons, it is believed that some of these protocols
cannot be implemented
