\emph{3.1. The bilinear Diffie--Hellman assumption}

BDH was originally defined in the symmetric setting {[}8{]} and later
extended to the asymmetric setting {[}26,13{]}. It is possible to define
several versions of the problem in the asymmetric setting --- see e.g.,
{[}37,12{]} and Remark 2. We consider the following version of the
problem in Type 2 used by Galindo in {[}26{]} and which is the same as
the problem discussed in {[}13{]} when specialized to Type 2.

